// could force an allocation of up to `kMaxLength` bytes. The overlap check
// counters the "quoted overlap" zip-bomb shape (CVE-2024-0450 in other
// implementations): N records quoting the same data region turn one small file
// into N full-size extractions, while real archives lay members out
// disjointly. The exact data range depends on the local header's length, which
// is read here (one small read per member) so the check matches the read path
// and the in-memory reader (`readArchiveEntries()`) rather than trusting a
// looser lower bound.
